Args.CodeContent:
# Implementation Plan - CSS Separation & Organization

This plan outlines the process of extracting the inline CSS from `3_new26.html` and organizing it into clean, modular, and maintainable CSS files.

## Proposed Changes

To organize the styles, we will create a dedicated `css/` directory and split the CSS rules into files corresponding to their functional components.

### CSS Directory Structure

We will create the following files in the new `css/` directory:

1. **[base.css](file:///c:/Users/ifilm/OneDrive/à¹€à¸­à¸à¸ªà¸²à¸£/3_new26/css/base.css)** [NEW]
   - CSS resets, variables (`:root`), global `body` settings, and custom scrollbars.
2. **[layout.css](file:///c:/Users/ifilm/OneDrive/à¹€à¸­à¸à¸ªà¸²à¸£/3_new26/css/layout.css)** [NEW]
   - Main page layout containers, sidebar (`.sidebar`), top header (`.topbar`), buttons, and shared layout elements (like `.vuln-panel-title`).
3. **[vulnerability_status.css](file:///c:/Users/ifilm/OneDrive/à¹€à¸­à¸à¸ªà¸²à¸£/3_new26/css/vulnerability_status.css)** [NEW]
   - Styles for the **Vulnerability Status** section (`.vuln-panel`, `.outline-card`, etc.).
4. **[ticket_workflow.css](file:///c:/Users/ifilm/OneDrive/à¹€à¸­à¸à¸ªà¸²à¸£/3_new26/css/ticket_workflow.css)** [NEW]
   - Styles for the **Ticket Workflow** section (`.stat-card`, `.stats-grid`).
5. **[severity_distribution.css](file:///c:/Users/ifilm/OneDrive/à¹€à¸­à¸à¸ªà¸²à¸£/3_new26/css/severity_distribution.css)** [NEW]
   - Styles for the **Severity & Risk Distribution** arc gauges (`.severity-panel`, `.gauge-card`, etc.).
6. **[findings_table.css](file:///c:/Users/ifilm/OneDrive/à¹€à¸­à¸à¸ªà¸²à¸£/3_new26/css/findings_table.css)** [NEW]
   - Styles for the search bar, filter chips, the findings table, status badges, and pagination.
7. **[style.css](file:///c:/Users/ifilm/OneDrive/à¹€à¸­à¸à¸ªà¸²à¸£/3_new26/css/style.css)** [NEW]
   - The entry point stylesheet that uses `@import` to load the modular CSS files in the correct order:
     ```css
     @import 'base.css';
     @import 'layout.css';
     @import 'vulnerability_status.css';
     @import 'ticket_workflow.css';
     @import 'severity_distribution.css';
     @import 'findings_table.css';
     ```

### HTML Modification

We will modify:
- **[3_new26.html](file:///c:/Users/ifilm/OneDrive/à¹€à¸­à¸à¸ªà¸²à¸£/3_new26/3_new26.html)** [MODIFY]
  - Remove the inline `<style>` block.
  - Link the entry point stylesheet using `<link rel="stylesheet" href="css/style.css">`.

---

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- We will open `3_new26.html` in the browser to verify that:
  - The page layout is identical to the original version.
  - Interactive elements (hover states, active chips, line-item highlights) look and behave correctly.
  - Responsive alignment functions properly.

