Args.CodeContent:
# Fix Nginx Gateway DNS Caching Issue

During testing of the microservices orchestration, we identified a critical issue with independent container lifecycle operations. 

When a service (e.g., `hub`, `defectdojo`, or `wazuh`) is restarted or rebuilt, Docker assigns it a new internal IP address. However, the Nginx gateway caches the IP address resolved at startup. Subsequent requests to the service result in `502 Bad Gateway` (with `Host is unreachable` or `Connection refused` in the Nginx error log) until the Nginx gateway container is manually restarted.

This plan details how we will resolve this issue to support independent container startups and shutdowns.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This change resolves the 502 Bad Gateway issues caused by Docker IP address reassignments. The gateway will dynamically re-resolve the IP addresses of backends using Docker's internal DNS resolver (`127.0.0.11`) with a 5-second TTL.

## Proposed Changes

### Nginx Gateway Component

#### [MODIFY] [nginx.conf](file:///c:/Users/ifilm/à¹€à¸”à¸ªà¸à¹Œà¸—à¹‡à¸­à¸›/Scan%20CSV%20File/defectdojo-viewer/gateway/nginx.conf)

We will modify the Nginx config to:
1. Declare Docker's internal DNS resolver `127.0.0.11` with a short TTL (`valid=5s`).
2. Store the backend URLs in variables (e.g., `$hub_upstream`, `$defectdojo_upstream`, `$wazuh_upstream`).
3. Use rewrite directives (`rewrite`) to strip path prefixes (like `/defectdojo/` and `/wazuh/`) before proxy passing, because Nginx does not perform automatic path stripping when `proxy_pass` contains a variable.

Here is the proposed configuration:

```nginx
# Rate limiting zone for auth endpoints
limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=login_limit:10m rate=5r/s;

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name localhost;

    # Dynamic DNS resolution using Docker's resolver
    resolver 127.0.0.11 valid=5s;

    # Security Headers
    add_header X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN" always;
    add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;
    add_header X-XSS-Protection "1; mode=block" always;
    add_header Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" always;

    # Enable gzip compression
    gzip on;
    gzip_types text/plain text/css application/json application/javascript text/xml application/xml application/xml+rss text/javascript;
    gzip_min_length 1000;

    # â”€â”€ 1. HUB SERVICE (ROOT) â”€â”€
    location / {
        set $hub_upstream http://hub:3000;
        proxy_pass $hub_upstream;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;

        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }

    # Rate-limit the Hub login endpoint to prevent brute-force attacks
    location = /api/login {
        limit_req zone=login_limit burst=10 nodelay;

        set $hub_upstream http://hub:3000;
        proxy_pass $hub_upstream;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }

    # Disable buffering for Server-Sent Events (SSE) sync stream
    location /defectdojo/api/sync/events {
        rewrite ^/defectdojo/(.*)$ /$1 break;
        set $defectdojo_upstream http://defectdojo:3001;
        proxy_pass $defectdojo_upstream;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;

        # SSE Buffering Prevention
        proxy_buffering off;
        proxy_cache off;
        chunked_transfer_encoding on;
        proxy_read_timeout 86400s;
    }

    # â”€â”€ 2. DEFECTDOJO VIEWER SERVICE â”€â”€
    location /defectdojo/ {
        rewrite ^/defectdojo/(.*)$ /$1 break;
        set $defectdojo_upstream http://defectdojo:3001;
        proxy_pass $defectdojo_upstream;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;

        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;

        # Adjust cookies path if the backend uses session cookies (fallback safety)
        proxy_cookie_path / /defectdojo;
    }

    # â”€â”€ 3. WAZUH VIEWER SERVICE (MOCKUP) â”€â”€
    location /wazuh/ {
        rewrite ^/wazuh/(.*)$ /$1 break;
        set $wazuh_upstream http://wazuh:3002;
        proxy_pass $wazuh_upstream;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;

        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }

    # Error handling configuration
    error_page 502 /502.html;
    location = /502.html {
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
        internal;
        # Inline custom styled error message fitting the design system
        return 502 '{"error": "Bad Gateway - The requested middleware service is temporarily offline or rebuilding. Please try again in a few moments."}';
    }
}
```

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
We will run lifecycle commands to confirm that Nginx dynamically resolves services:
1. Restart the `hub` container: `docker compose restart hub`
2. Test requesting `http://localhost/api/health`. It must resolve correctly immediately.
3. Rebuild and restart `defectdojo`: `docker compose up -d --build --remove-orphans defectdojo`
4. Test requesting `http://localhost/defectdojo/api/health`. It must resolve correctly immediately.
5. Restart `wazuh`: `docker compose restart wazuh`
6. Test requesting `http://localhost/wazuh/`. It must resolve correctly immediately.

